   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:small\">Hi,</div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:small\"><br></div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:small\">I am trying to run BSM on my data with a DEC+x+j model and it worked well until the final PDF. When I run the plot_BioGeoBEARS_results() function it returns the following error:</div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:small\"><br></div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:small\"><div class=\"gmail_default\"> Error in rangestxt_to_colors(possible_ranges_list_txt, colors_list_for_states,  : </div><div class=\"gmail_default\">  Error: possible_ranges_list_txt and colors_list_for_states must be the same length </div><div class=\"gmail_default\"><br></div><div class=\"gmail_default\">Does anyone know what that means?</div><div class=\"gmail_default\">Thanks in advance.</div><div class=\"gmail_default\">Cheers,</div></div><div><div class=\"gmail_signature\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div style=\"font-family:garamond,serif;font-size:large\"><br></div><div><span style=\"font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:small\">-----------------------------------------------------------------</span></div><div><font size=\"2\" face=\"arial, helvetica, sans-serif\"><b>Gabriel S. Ferreira</b> - </font><span style=\"font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:small\">PhD Student</span><br></div><div><font size=\"2\"><div style=\"text-align:center\"><div style=\"text-align:left\"><span style=\"font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif\">Phone: <a href=\"tel:+55%2016%203315-4984\" value=\"+551633154984\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\">+55-16-3315 4984</a></span><font face=\"arial, helvetica, sans-serif\"><br></font></div><div style=\"text-align:left\"><font face=\"arial, helvetica, sans-serif\"><br></font></div><div style=\"text-align:left\"><font face=\"arial, helvetica, sans-serif\"><a href=\"http://sites.ffclrp.usp.br/paleo/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://sites.ffclrp.usp.br/paleo/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792484803703000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0p95xOCP9O2nOpFyge6UzU\">PaleoLab</a>, Uni. São Paulo, </font><span style=\"font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif\">Ribeirão Preto, </span><span style=\"font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif\">Brazil</span></div></div><div style=\"text-align:left\"><font face=\"arial, helvetica, sans-serif\">Eberhard Karls Universität </font><span style=\"font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif\">Tübingen/Germany</span><br></div><div style=\"text-align:left\"><font face=\"arial, helvetica, sans-serif\">-----------------------------------------------------------------</font></div><div style=\"text-align:left\"><font face=\"arial, helvetica, sans-serif\"><br></font></div><div style=\"text-align:left\"><font face=\"arial, helvetica, sans-serif\">&#39;Form is a moving, a becoming, a passing thing. The doctrine of forms is the doctrine of transformation. The doctrine of metamorphosis is the key to all signs of nature&#39; J.W. von Goethe<br></font><br><br></div></font></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div>\r\n</div>\r\n"
    ]
