     "<div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:small\">Hi,</div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:small\"><br></div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:small\">I am trying to run BSM on my data with a DEC+x+j model and it worked well until the final PDF. When I run the plot_BioGeoBEARS_results() function it returns the following error:</div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:small\"><br></div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:small\"><div class=\"gmail_default\"> Error in rangestxt_to_colors(possible_ranges_list_txt, colors_list_for_states,  : </div><div class=\"gmail_default\">  Error: possible_ranges_list_txt and colors_list_for_states must be the same length </div><div class=\"gmail_default\"><br></div><div class=\"gmail_default\">Does anyone know what that means?</div><div class=\"gmail_default\">Thanks in advance.</div><div class=\"gmail_default\">Cheers,</div></div><div><div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div style=\"font-family:garamond,serif;font-size:large\"><br></div><div><span style=\"font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:small\">-----------------------------------------------------------------</span></div><div><font size=\"2\" face=\"arial, helvetica, sans-serif\"><b>Gabriel S. Ferreira</b> - </font><span style=\"font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:small\">PhD Student</span><br></div><div><font size=\"2\"><div style=\"text-align:center\"><div style=\"text-align:left\"><span style=\"font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif\">Phone: <a href